After each worker return or your own repair cycle, before adding a supporting dependency to the critical path, and when a supplier reports a new blocker, reassess what the work changed, or would change, about the effort's unresolved question or acceptance evidence. As the direct overseer, apply this check to the parent outcome. Distinguish requirements of that outcome from conditions of the chosen implementation and optional improvements; compare the smallest existing qualified method. When work changes only the method without a grounded reason it is needed for the outcome, change route: simplify, take a discriminating observation, change the hypothesis, repair a defect blocking a named observation, or escalate a concrete need. A method-only return or long review alone proves neither drift nor necessity. Choose one bounded authorized action, continue necessary work for an evidence-grounded reason, or present the consequential choice through the operator's attention channel and await the answer. Preserve genuine holds and unknown outcomes.
